  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Drag sensitivity - changes sensitivity of slope changes, larger value
    means faster, but less precise changes

    Respect original slopes - when it''s
    on, slopes are added on top of existing ones. When off, all slopes are changed
    to single value (area becomes flat)


    1. Drag mouse to select area you want
    to edit, shift-click to select multiple areas. Right-click while selecting cancels
    current selection, otherwise it deselects selected area

    2. Click handle
    inside selected area to make it an anchor. Moving pointer in any direction anchors
    entire axis instead, represented with red line appearing. Anchor is point (or
    axis) which won''t change its height in later step

    3. Drag any handle inside
    selected area and move pointer up/down to make ramp from that point to anchor


    Right-click
    during any action cancels the action. Otherwise, if there is an anchor it gets
    deselected, and if the anchor doesn''t exist area gets deselected'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
